../types.ts
types.ts

# Output
export default class SviDependencyCycleAnalyzer

# Options
Active=True

# Import prompts
sviFileOrderOptimizerPrompt.svi

# Prompt
The main purpose of this class is to analyze dependencies and find cycled dependencies.
Cycled dependencies is when a file depends on the other, and the other depends on the
first one explicitly or through a chain of other dependencies.

Methods of class

* constructor(sviDependencies: SviDependency[])
Stores in an attribute

* findCycles
Analyzes the sviDependencies[] array and prepares structures necessary for other methods

* isFileInCycle(sviFile : SVIFile) : boolean
If the file is contained in at least one cycle, then return true

* areFilesInTheSameCycle(sviFile1 : SVIFile, sviFile2 : SVIFile) : boolean

If both files are contained in the same dependency cycle, then return true

Recommended imports:
```ts
import { SVIFile, SviFileToLoad, ImportPromptPath } from "../types";
import { SviDependency } from "./types";
```